    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0456" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg386"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Campbell</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 27, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatches Nos. 20 and
                    21, of the 18th and 20th instant, together with a memorial addressed to the
                    United States government from certain authorities and generals of the district
                    of Tampico, transmitted to you by Mr. Chase, the consul general at that city.
                    The views of this government on the subject of the memorial have been explained
                    to Mr. Chase in a communication, a copy of which is sent you herewith for your
                    information. As regards the request of Mr. Chase to have a United States war
                    vessel stationed at Tampico, it has been submitted to the Secretary of the
                    Navy.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis D. Campbell,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d262-a1.xml" xpointer="d262-a1"/>
